{{!< default}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>The Library Reader | The Faith Received</title>
<meta name="description" content="Read the early modern theological library of The Faith Received, thousands of works in a clean reader." />
<meta property="og:title" content="The Library Reader | The Faith Received" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Read the early modern theological library of The Faith Received, thousands of works in a clean reader." />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="The Library Reader | The Faith Received" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Read the early modern theological library of The Faith Received, thousands of works in a clean reader." />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- Dynamic reader for The Faith Received library works.
     URL: /the-faith-received/reader/?w=slug&c=corpus

     Rebuilt 2026-08-21. The header was the last surface wearing the
     old magazine chrome: a full-bleed dark hero with a 72px display
     title, centred, which pushed the first line of text most of a
     screen down and truncated any title over 64 characters into an
     ellipsis with the rest hidden in a tooltip.

     It is now a title page rather than a hero. The plate colour and
     kicker come from the TFR band language so the reader belongs to
     the same product as the rooms, but it is set at reading scale,
     left-aligned on the reading measure, and it carries the work's
     categories and its introduction where every work has them in the
     same place.

     Every data-fr-* and data-faith-* hook here is read by
     faith-reader.js or faith-reader-tools.js. Check both before
     removing one. --}}

<main class="article faith-doc faith-doc--library faith-doc--books faith-doc--editorial faith-reader">

  <div class="article-body faith-doc-body faith-doc-body--has-sidebar">
    <div class="faith-doc-layout">

      {{!-- Contents. Far left of the window on desktop, a drawer on
            mobile.

            The backdrop is not decoration. Below 1024px the drawer
            covers the page and `body` scrolling is frozen, and both
            faith-received.css and faith-received.js have always
            expected a [data-faith-toc-backdrop] to close it. The
            generated document partials ship one; this template did
            not, so tapping away did nothing and the close button
            scrolled out of reach on any long contents list. --}}
      <div class="faith-toc-backdrop" data-faith-toc-backdrop hidden></div>
      <aside class="faith-toc-sidebar" data-faith-toc-drawer aria-label="Document contents">
        {{!-- Header row stays put while the list scrolls under it, so
              the way out is always on screen. --}}
        <div class="faith-toc-bar">
          <p class="faith-toc-bar-label">Contents</p>
          <button type="button" class="faith-toc-close" data-faith-toc-close aria-label="Close contents">
            <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <nav class="faith-toc faith-toc--books" aria-label="Contents" data-fr-toc>
          <p class="faith-toc-label-heading">Contents</p>
          <p class="faith-toc-loading">Loading contents&hellip;</p>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <div class="faith-doc-inner">

        {{!-- ── The work's title page ──────────────────────────── --}}
        <header class="faith-reader-head">
          <p class="faith-reader-kicker">
            <a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a>
            <span class="faith-reader-kicker-sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
            <a href="/the-faith-received/browse/" data-fr-collection>The Library</a>
          </p>

          <h1 class="faith-reader-title" data-fr-title>Loading&hellip;</h1>
          <p class="faith-reader-subtitle" data-fr-subtitle hidden></p>

          <p class="faith-reader-byline" data-fr-dek></p>
          <p class="faith-reader-translator" data-fr-translator></p>

          {{!-- Every category the catalogue knows about this work:
                collection, tradition and its parent, century, kind,
                region. Built by faith-reader.js. --}}
          <ul class="faith-reader-tags" data-fr-tags>
            <li hidden><a href="/the-faith-received/browse/#traditions" class="faith-reader-tag" data-fr-tradition></a></li>
          </ul>

          {{!-- How this work was made and how far it has been checked.
                Above the introduction on purpose: a reader deciding
                whether to trust a machine translation should meet that
                fact before the text, not after it. Filled by
                faith-work-status.js. --}}
          <div class="faith-reader-status" data-fr-status hidden></div>

          {{!-- The introduction. One place, every work: the corpus
                blurb where there is one, the catalogue description
                otherwise. --}}
          <div class="faith-reader-intro" data-fr-intro hidden>
            <p class="faith-reader-intro-text" data-fr-description></p>
          </div>

          <div class="faith-doc-actions">
            <button type="button" class="faith-doc-toc-toggle" data-faith-toc-toggle aria-label="Open contents">
              <span class="faith-doc-toc-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <span></span><span></span><span></span>
              </span>
              <span class="faith-doc-toc-toggle-label">Contents</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          {{!-- "Make a reading plan". Last inside the title-page header
                on purpose, and specifically AFTER .faith-doc-actions:
                that div carries a 22px top margin and 40px of height for
                a Contents button that is mobile-only, so anything placed
                above it sits 86px clear of the rule below while being
                23px from the rule above. Down here the only thing under
                it is the header's own 24px of padding, which matches.

                Renders only for people who are not signed in;
                faith-plan.js returns immediately when body carries
                data-member-email. --}}
          <div class="faith-plan-mount" data-fr-plan
               data-plans-url="https://mo-tfr-plans.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev"></div>
        </header>

        {{!-- Loading state --}}
        <div class="faith-reader-loading" data-fr-loading>
          <p class="faith-reader-loading-text">Loading work&hellip;</p>
        </div>

        {{!-- Error state --}}
        <div class="faith-reader-error" data-fr-error hidden>
          <p class="faith-reader-error-text">Could not load this work. Please check the URL and try again.</p>
        </div>

        {{!-- Content container: sections rendered here by JS --}}
        <section class="faith-books-section faith-lang-en" aria-label="Content" data-fr-content>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
        {{!-- ── The tools ───────────────────────────────────────
       A dock, fixed at the bottom right, rather than a row at
       the top of the work. A row at the top is only reachable
       from the top: a reader four hundred pages down who wants
       larger type, or the contents, or the way back, had to
       scroll all the way up to ask for it.
       
       The mount points inside are unchanged, because other files
       own them: faith-reader-tools.js appends Find and Notebook
       to [data-faith-controls], faith-reader-prefs.js mounts
       into [data-faith-prefs], and faith-reader.js rebuilds the
       language buttons from the corpus's declared lanes, so the
       three below are only the Latin defaults shown before the
       work's meta arrives. --}}
  <div class="faith-dock" data-faith-dock>
    <button type="button" class="faith-dock-btn faith-dock-top" data-faith-dock-top hidden
            aria-label="Back to the top of the work">
      <span aria-hidden="true">&uarr;</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="faith-dock-btn faith-dock-contents" data-faith-dock-contents
            aria-label="Contents">
      <span aria-hidden="true">&#9776;</span>
    </button>
    {{!-- A pill rather than a circle: "Aa" alone is a guess unless you
          already know what it opens, and this is the control the whole
          set of reading tools hangs off. The rule between the two is
          drawn in CSS so it cannot be read aloud as punctuation. --}}
    {{!-- Support. A membership prompt belongs where a reader's hands
          already are, not at the foot of an eight-hundred-page folio
          that almost nobody reaches. Same paid/comped gate as every
          other membership prompt on the site. --}}
    {{#match @member.status "paid"}}{{else}}
    {{#match @member.status "comped"}}{{else}}
    <a href="/membership/" class="faith-dock-btn faith-dock-support" data-hm-goal="member-cta">Support</a>
    {{/match}}
    {{/match}}
    <button type="button" class="faith-dock-btn faith-dock-toggle" data-faith-dock-toggle
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faith-dock-panel" aria-label="Text tools">
      <span class="faith-dock-aa" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span>
      <span class="faith-dock-toggle-label" aria-hidden="true">Text Tools</span>
    </button>
  <div class="faith-reading-controls faith-toolbar" id="faith-dock-panel" data-faith-controls hidden>
    <button type="button" class="faith-tool" data-faith-expand-toggle aria-pressed="false">
      <span class="faith-toggle-label" data-off="Expand all" data-on="Collapse all">Expand all</span>
    </button>

    <div class="faith-lang-toggle" data-faith-lang-toggle hidden role="group" aria-label="Language">
      <button type="button" class="faith-lang-btn" data-lang="en" aria-pressed="true">English</button>
      <button type="button" class="faith-lang-btn" data-lang="la" aria-pressed="false">Latin</button>
      <button type="button" class="faith-lang-btn" data-lang="parallel" aria-pressed="false">Parallel</button>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="faith-tool faith-modernizer-toggle" data-modernizer-toggle aria-pressed="false" hidden>
      <span class="faith-toggle-label faith-modernizer-label" data-off="Original spelling" data-on="Modern spelling">Original spelling</span>
    </button>

    {{!-- Reading preferences: type size, face, line spacing,
          measure. Mounted by faith-reader-prefs.js. --}}
    <div class="faith-prefs" data-faith-prefs></div>
  </div>
  </div>

</main>


{{!-- CDN base URL for fetching work data. Read by faith-reader.js.
     Uses a <meta> tag instead of inline JS so the CSP can remain
     free of 'unsafe-inline' on script-src. --}}
<meta name="tfr-library-base" content="https://mo-tfr-library.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-modernize.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-corpora.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-century.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-received.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- Matches a scripture reference against early modern printing, so a
     citation link from the index can land on the line rather than on
     the title page. Loaded before the reader, which calls it as soon as
     a work renders. --}}
{{!-- What counts as a match: whole words, not letters inside words.
     Shared with the searches on the browse and author pages. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-text.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-scripture-ref.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-reader.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- "Report An Issue" in the text tools: a reader who has found a bad
     translation or a broken page is already looking at it, so the form
     comes to them and carries the work with it. Appended to the same
     controls the reader's own tools use, so it loads after them. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-report-issue.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-work-status.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- The citation resolver exposes window.MOResolve here rather than
     any UI: an arriving constellation addresses Patrologia Graeca by
     volume and column, and the resolver is what turns that into the
     work and anchor we hold. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-resolve.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- Find in work + notebook. Loaded after the reader so the tools
     mount over rendered content.

     The store FIRST, and it is not optional: it holds the notebook's
     only definition of the stored format, the citation format, and the
     constellation wire format, shared with the Notebook workspace
     (partials/faith-received/_notebook-panel.hbs). Without it
     faith-reader-tools.js still gives the reader Find, and says in the
     console that the notebook is missing. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/lib/faith-notebook-store.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-reader-tools.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-reader-prefs.js"}}"></script>
{{!-- Docks the tools at the bottom right and keeps them there. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-dock.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-bookmark.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-plan.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-gate.js"}}"></script>
